ml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(5071.8,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D714\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D714\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(5693.8,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D461\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D461\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(6277,0)\"><use data-c=\"2212\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2212\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(7277.2,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D458\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D458\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(7798.2,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D465\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D465\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(8370.2,0)\"><use data-c=\"29\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-29\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>, the ratio of average electric energy density to average magnetic energy density is</p>","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"1"},{"identifier":"B","content":"4"},{"identifier":"C","content":"2"},{"identifier":"D","content":"1/2"}],"correct_options":["A"],"explanation":"<p>The average energy density of an electromagnetic wave is equally shared between the electric field and the magnetic field. This means that the average electric energy density is equal to the average magnetic energy density. </p>\n<p>The average electric energy density (<mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.339ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"2.704ex\" height=\"1.339ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -442 1195.2 592\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D462\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D462\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(605,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"1D438\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D438\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>) is given by:</